    "title": "Special Weather Statement by NWS - NewsBreak",
    "text": "4 minutes ago Check NWS updates here\nEffective: 2025-09-03 23:28:00 CDT Expires: 2025-09-04 00:00:00 CDT Urgency: Expected Severity: Moderate Certainty: Observed Instruction: If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building. Target Area: Gibson; Posey; Vanderburgh At 1127 PM CDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm near Cynthiana, or 10 miles southwest of Fort Branch, moving east at 40 mph.\nHAZARD...Wind gusts up to 40 mph and pea size hail.\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around unsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is possible.\nLocations impacted include... Evansville, Haubstadt, Darmstadt, and Cynthiana.\nThis includes the following highways... Interstate 69 in Indiana between Mile Markers 13 and 25. Interstate 64 in Indiana between Mile Markers 14 and 29.",
